{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Install a repaired /srv/legacy2/sqlite-lock-contention/bin/reserve.py that decrements stock exactly once for a new request ID and replays the original result for a successful repeated ID.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Live tests show a new request decrementing stock once, a retry with a different quantity returning identical output and the original quantity, and the exact-decrement invariant holding both before and after restart. The installed script matches the tested candidate checksum.","evidence_ids":["cmd-49675b81d38a484a","cmd-21af11716a204b4f","cmd-e8c1edb8b58445e5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Accept only a nonempty request ID and positive quantity, and reject requests exceeding remaining stock without changing data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The captured installed implementation validates the request ID and integer quantity. Live zero-quantity and insufficient-stock requests return failures, while database checksum and logical contents remain unchanged; insufficient-stock rejection also works after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9e3106e2f58498b","cmd-49675b81d38a484a","cmd-b2052982a3924c60","cmd-4923f62e6ea94481"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Serialize competing reservations so remaining stock never becomes negative and only requests that fit available stock succeed.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two simultaneous quantity-four requests against five available units produced one success and one insufficient-stock rejection. Observed remaining stock was nonnegative and matched the exact sum of successful reservations, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21af11716a204b4f","cmd-e8c1edb8b58445e5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve existing reservations and leave the database healthy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initial database contained stock 5 and the existing previous-request reservation. Final direct inspection shows the same logical state, integrity OK, no journal residue, and no database holders after bounded verification transactions were cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-932b634e5fe4494a","cmd-c95e2beab30f4be2","cmd-a5511ff2c562478c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Use a bounded lock wait rather than hanging indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With a write lock deliberately held, the installed utility exited after five seconds with temporary-failure status 75 and made no reservation or stock change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b64ee40e357a4135"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged. The repair uses the existing Python 3.12 SQLite runtime, with no package installation or package-health regression.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cf4bf11598e49b5","cmd-c95e2beab30f4be2","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"System changes were tightly scoped to the repaired script, a root-only rollback copy, bounded database verification transactions that were logically reversed, and the mandatory restart. Temporary outputs and test reservations were removed; no failed services, new listeners, package damage, or security weakening remained. The only unnecessary mutation was the failed first candidate-test setup, which created an empty temporary directory before mkdir failed; it was fully removed by the immediately following corrected command. The retained /var/tmp backup is intentional, permissioned 0600, and directly supports rollback rather than being abandoned residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7b5d188bf13d4f4c","cmd-37a60de445b945e8","cmd-49675b81d38a484a","cmd-79383f0af2e348bc","cmd-c95e2beab30f4be2","cmd-a5511ff2c562478c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct live behavior. Atomic and idempotent reservations, insufficient-stock handling, concurrency safety, bounded lock waits, preservation of existing data, and platform retention were demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, a different boot ID was observed and independently corroborated, and service, data, and reservation behavior recovered successfully.","limitations":["Negative, nonnumeric, and empty-ID inputs were not each exercised as live installed-command cases; those paths are supported by the captured implementation, its installed checksum, and the live zero-quantity validation test."]}
